<div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose about">
  <p class="lead">Canlander.org is a community-run guide for players who are new to Canadian Highlander, or who've heard about it and want to know what the fuss is about.</p>

  <h2>What we are</h2>
  <p>A place to learn the format, find the good links, and keep up with points changes without digging through a Discord channel. We write for someone who knows how Magic works but has never built a 100-card singleton deck.</p>

  <h2>What we're not</h2>
  <p>We're not the official site. The rules and the points list are kept by the Canlander Council at <a href="{{ site.official.home }}">canadianhighlander.ca</a>. When they publish something, we summarize it and link to it. If we ever get something wrong, they're right and we'll fix it.</p>
  <p>We're also not affiliated with Wizards of the Coast.</p>

  <h2>Helping out</h2>
  <p>The site is open source. Every link on the <a href="/resources/">Resources</a> page lives in one small data file, and every news post is a plain text file. If you'd like to add a resource, fix a typo, or write something for newer players, you can <a href="{{ site.repo }}">open an issue or pull request on GitHub</a>.</p>

  <h2>Thanks</h2>
  <p>To the players in Victoria, BC who started all this in 1999 and kept it going, to the council volunteers who keep the points list honest, and to everyone running weeklies, recording podcasts, and logging results.</p>
</div>
